From 28b4737303d55a011e7ba0253f10f70cd1d76fb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:36:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NXForge: band-limited sample reading in the MP2K shadow mixer

The MP2K HLE mixer read each instrument sample with a straight line between
neighbouring samples. That leaves mirror images of the instrument above its
own Nyquist (the fizz on top of GBA music) and dulls its real top end, and a
pitched-up voice folds its highs back down as aliasing. interp.rs evaluates a
16-tap Kaiser-windowed sinc instead, centred on the play head (no delay),
stretched for voices that play faster than the 65536 Hz grid, with the
weights normalised so a constant stays constant. DPCM voices keep two decoded
blocks so the window can straddle a block edge. RECOMP_MP2K_LINEAR=1 brings
back the old reader for A/B listening.
---
